            <div xml:id="d826">

                <pb facs="0703" n="691" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg691"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.51/1285: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-05T17:00:00-04:00">December 5, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:06 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>296. Referring to the Embassy’s telegram No. 294, December 4, 5 p.m., the Foreign
                        Minister<anchor n="35" xml:id="d826-f1"/> this morning handed me a note on
                    suspension of amortization insisting that action embarrassing but forced by
                    circumstances and in no remote sense more than temporary suspension. Note going
                    forward by pouch today.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d826-f1" n="35" xml:id="d826-f1-content">
                <p>Abraham Ortega.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
